  "prompt": "Compare the shade on the block across Eastern Parkway from the 18-story building proposed at 1550 Bedford Avenue in Crown Heights, Brooklyn, between Franklin Avenue and Bedford Avenue, without and with that building, as two scenarios. Use the Crown Heights dataset in the catalog: NYC's building footprints with their roof heights in metres, that block's outline and the site's lot, and the street centerlines with their roadway widths. In the scenario with the building, add it to the buildings as an edit a user can change on a map: its base to 135 feet on the lot, set back 30 feet from Eastern Parkway, and its upper floors to 185 feet, set back above the base, 10 feet from Eastern Parkway and Bedford Avenue and 15 feet from Union Street. Count a day from an hour and a half after sunrise to an hour and a half before sunset, in New York time, every 10 minutes, with sunrise and sunset from the suntime library and the sun's position from astral. Let the user pick one day of 2027, the spring equinox, the summer solstice, the fall equinox or the winter solstice, and also count every day of 2027 the same way. Cover the area with 3 metre cells and keep only the open ground, outside the buildings. On the GPU, in each scenario, find how long each ground cell spends in the shadow of any building on the day picked, and the share of the block's open ground in shadow at each step of that day and of every day of the year. Map each scenario's shadow and the shade the proposed building adds on the day picked, with the block highlighted, the proposed building in its own color and the streets; plot the block's share in shadow through the day picked, a line per scenario, with the day's window under it; plot the block's time in shadow on each day of the year, a line per scenario; and show in a table, for each month, the shade the building adds to the block a day, as the month's average and standard deviation.",
  "context": null,
  "required": {
    "datasets": [
      "data.nyc.crown-heights-1550-bedford"
