  "notes": "Fixed context: three data loaders (buildings, Block 1259 and streets), a Python node holding the Day widget that lists the day's sun steps and another that lists every day of 2027's alike (suntime and astral), the open-ground grid and the maps' extent. Two scenarios: without the proposed building, and with it, whose lever is a Map Editor node adding the building in two parts, linked to its scenario's map by an interaction edge. In each, a Python node draws the scenario's buildings into a heights grid, and three Autark compute steps march from the ground toward the sun across it: one gives each cell's minutes in shadow on the day picked, the two others the share of Block 1259's open ground in shadow at each step of that day and of the year. Python nodes read them, keep the shaded cells for the scenario's map, and add up each day of the year. Outside the scenarios a Python node takes the shade the proposed building adds per cell for a third map, another averages the shade it adds on the block a day over each month, with the standard deviation, for a Simple View, and two Vega-Lite plots draw both scenarios from the stacked inputs: the share through the day picked, with its window, and the time in shadow each day of the year."
}
